# {{ .input_root_dir }}

This directory contains a [Kedro](https://docs.kedro.org) project wired to deploy and run
on Databricks as an [asset bundle]({{ template `generate_doc_link` (map (pair "path" "dev-tools/bundles/index.html")) }}).
Each Kedro node becomes a task in a Databricks job, so the same pipeline code runs locally
and on a cluster.

The job definitions are generated from the Kedro pipelines by
[kedro-databricks](https://github.com/JenspederM/kedro-databricks), which means the
Databricks workflow follows the pipeline rather than being maintained alongside it.

## Code structure

This project contains the following components:

| Component            | Description                                                                                                                                                                                          |
|----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Kedro pipelines      | Example ML pipeline code as unit-tested Python nodes, with a data catalog and parameters per environment                                                                                              |
| ML Resources as Code | Databricks jobs, a Unity Catalog registered model, an MLflow experiment and an opt-in quality monitor, configured and deployed through [databricks CLI bundles]({{ template `generate_doc_link` (map (pair "path" "dev-tools/cli/bundle-cli.html")) }}) |

contained in the following files:

```
{{ .input_root_dir }}        <- Root directory. Both monorepo and polyrepo are supported.
│
└── {{template `project_name_alphanumeric_underscore` .}}       <- One Kedro project: pipeline code, config and Databricks resources.
    │
    ├── databricks.yml          <- Bundle root file loaded by the databricks CLI. Defines the bundle
    │                              name, variables, the wheel artifact, the conf sync rules, and the
    │                              dev/staging/prod/test deployment targets.
    │
    ├── pyproject.toml          <- Project metadata and dependencies. [project.scripts] declares the
    │                              console script that the Databricks tasks invoke; [tool.kedro] declares
    │                              the package name. Dependencies are managed by uv.
    │
    ├── uv.lock                 <- Locked dependency versions for reproducible installs (generated by uv).
    │
    ├── conf                    <- Kedro configuration.
    │   ├── base                <- Shared across every environment: catalog.yml, parameters.yml.
    │   ├── local               <- Personal credentials and overrides. Not committed.
    │   ├── dev, staging, prod, test
    │   │                       <- One directory per deployment target. catalog.yml points datasets at
    │   │                          that target's storage; databricks.yml holds the cluster, schedule and
    │   │                          job-name overrides that are merged into resources/ at generation time.
    │   └── logging.yml
    │
    ├── data                    <- Kedro's layered data directories. Real data lives in the workspace.
    │
    ├── src/{{template `project_name_alphanumeric_underscore` .}}
    │   ├── pipeline_registry.py <- Discovers the pipelines under pipelines/.
    │   ├── settings.py          <- Config loader setup, including the `databricks` config pattern.
    │   └── pipelines            <- The pipelines themselves. Most development work happens here.
    │       └── iris             <- Example pipeline: nodes.py and pipeline.py.
    │
    ├── monitoring              <- Notebooks used by the opt-in quality monitoring resource.
    │
    ├── notebooks               <- Ad-hoc notebooks.
    │
    ├── tests                   <- Unit tests for the pipelines.
    │
    └── resources               <- Databricks resource definitions.
        ├── {{template `project_name_alphanumeric_underscore` .}}.yml
        │                       <- GENERATED. Job for the `__default__` Kedro pipeline, one task per node.
        ├── ml-artifacts-resource.yml
        │                       <- Unity Catalog registered model and MLflow experiment.
        └── monitoring/monitoring-resource.yml
                                <- Opt-in quality monitor and retraining job. Nested one level down so
                                   that it is not picked up by the `resources/*.yml` include glob.
```

## Using this repo

If you are a data scientist starting a brand new ML project, adapt the example iris
pipeline to your problem, then make and test changes locally before deploying. Follow the
instructions in the [project README](./{{template `project_name_alphanumeric_underscore` .}}/README.md).

| Role           | Goal                                                                   | Docs                                                                                                          |
|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Data Scientist | Get started writing pipeline code for a brand new project              | [project README](./{{template `project_name_alphanumeric_underscore` .}}/README.md)                           |
| Data Scientist | Add or change pipeline nodes and regenerate the Databricks jobs        | [ML resource config guide](./{{template `project_name_alphanumeric_underscore` .}}/resources/README.md)       |
| MLOps / DevOps | Change compute, schedules, permissions or deployment targets           | [ML resource config guide](./{{template `project_name_alphanumeric_underscore` .}}/resources/README.md)       |
